young black people.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:44.364
But do you feel positive about
how much the movement's grow

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the years since
that first started?

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:51.004
-Sure. I mean, you know, first I
just want to send a lot of lov

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:54.741
and condolences to so many black
people who lost their live

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the hands of law enforcemen
and vigilantes.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:01.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
So much of our work is about
not just black death,

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:02.582 line:92%
but the fight for black life

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:07.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
And right now we're in a momen
where the entire country -

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:08.988 line:92%
and I argue the entire world -

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:12.792
is trying to reevaluate it
relationship to black people

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:15.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how much we're standing up
for black people

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:17.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how much we're fightin
for black people.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.066 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And I think my hope lies

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the very people
who are on the streets,

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:26.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
the people who I call essentia
workers for black life.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.440 line:92%
We're not just protesters.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.641 line:92%
We're working for black life

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're working to make sure tha
our children get to grow u

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:33.546
in a society where they're
not murdered or gunned dow

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:37.383
in their own neighborhoods o
in other people's neighborhoods.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.085 line:92%
I have a lot of hope right now

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:42.255 size:78% position:39%
even amidst the grief
and the rage I feel.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:46.025 size:88% position:44%
-The protests have been
overwhelmingly peaceful,

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:49.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there is a media focus
on looting.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:56.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, that makes for very
you know --

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want to say
good television,

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it feels like it ends up
on television a lot.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you were frustrated
by the fact

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:05.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
that oftentimes someone
like yourself,

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:08.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone who is supportive
of the protests,

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.148 line:92%
has to answer for the looting.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:13.820
How can people speak about
that element of it better,

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:17.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
or what are the questions
you would prefer to be asked

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.291 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Great question.

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:22.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think -- And what I'm ofte
describing to people

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:28.067 size:84% position:42%
is we are very obsessed
with property damage.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:33.072
Property damage is seen as
sort of like the pinnacle

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.741 line:92%
of destruction and violence.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:39.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we rarely hear the media
focus on police violence

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.079 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
or police terror.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:44.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
For example, Saturday,
many of us were out protesting

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.220 line:92%
across the country, me included.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was at a protest
in Los Angeles

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:50.390 size:81% position:41% line:92%
up at 3rd and Fairfax,

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was peaceful
for two hours.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:56.396
And then the police showed up,
and it was no longer peaceful.

00:04:56.396 --> 00:05:00.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
The police tear-gassed folks
They beat up people.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.602 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And it was unprovoked.

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:04.504 line:92%
And so there's this conversation

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:07.874
that I think is an uneven
conversation in the media

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:09.809 line:92%
about people who are looting

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:14.914
versus the infrastructure
and the structure of racis

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:15.648 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and the police officers

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:22.188
who continue to cause havo
and chaos in our communities

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:28.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ramy, you have been at some
of the protests visually,

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:31.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you have some pictures
we can share right now,

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:35.234 size:84% position:42%
because your billboard
is up for the new show.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:39.339
And let's be honest, you avoided
what could have been a lot worse

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:42.875 size:88% position:44%
based on show billboards
I've seen in the past.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.677 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Yeah. I mean, it's --

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:48.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, I've gotten a lot
of photos from close friends

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:50.283 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and I went myself, too.

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Man, this is a really --

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:54.921
I'm so happy we didn't pic
the picture of me smiling.

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:57.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was, like,
a big talk with marketing.

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:59.692
They're like, "No, you shoul
be smiling on the billboard.

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it would
look more inviting."

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:04.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm so glad
it's just that look down,

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:06.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it would be
kind of sinister

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:09.535
if I was smiling over everything
that's happening right now

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-But yeah, yeah.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That would have been
the rare case where you --

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:16.309 size:78% position:39%
It wouldn't have been
marketing's fault,

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:18.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you just
wouldn't have known

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:21.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
how bad a look
it would have been.

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:24.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also want to talk
about this idea

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:28.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I think people believe
to be radical,

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:31.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is when you hear
an activist

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:34.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
talk about the idea
of defunding the police.

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:39.699
But it is a less radical ide
than maybe people would jump to,

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:43.870
because it's not going fro
the current police budget

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:44.771 size:75% position:38% line:92%
to no police budget.

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:47.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
Could you just speak to
what that terminology mean

00:06:47.774 --> 00:06:51.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
and why most people
would probably agree with it

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.278 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure.

00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:57.784
If anybody has time, they should
look up their city budget.

00:06:57.784 --> 00:06:58.317 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's public.

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:03.356
And what they'll come to realize
across every major city --

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:05.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I argue small cities,
as well --

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:07.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that the majority
of the budgets

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:10.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
are made up of police,
of law enforcement,

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:12.031 line:92%
as a law enforcement budget.

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:15.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what we start to realize
so much

00:07:15.535 --> 00:07:18.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
in our communities
that are divested from,

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:19.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
that have little access
to healthcare,

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:24.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
educational opportunities,
access to jobs and healthy foo

00:07:24.043 --> 00:07:27.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that our city governments
are using our tax dollars

00:07:27.513 --> 00:07:31.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
to primarily pay for an econom
of punishment

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.685 size:88% position:44% line:92%
over an economy of care.

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:35.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's what so many
Black Lives Matter organizer

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:38.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
and organizers that are allies
of Black Lives Matter

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:44.330
are asking for is to allow for
a reallocation of investment

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:46.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
into some of
the most marginalized

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:48.367 line:92%
and divested-from communities.

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:51.671
-Ramy, I know you've been doin
comedy for a very long time.

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:55.675
Did you ever feel like even when
you talk about the issues

00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:57.643 size:75% position:38% line:92%
that you're helping?

00:07:57.643 --> 00:08:00.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think really the most
that I could do

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:05.618
or a show like mine could do
is emotionally prepare peopl

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:08.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
to face the questions
that they have.

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:11.257
I really don't think that comedy
is supposed to give answer

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:12.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
or that the work
can give answers,

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:14.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I think a lot of us
have questions

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:15.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we're afraid
to ask ourselves.

00:08:15.795 --> 00:08:17.096 line:92%
And I always hope that the wor

00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:19.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
can bring people closer
to those questions

00:08:19.198 --> 00:08:21.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
and closer to facing the thing
that they need to.

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:25.137
But to me, the real change comes
from people like Patrisse,

00:08:25.137 --> 00:08:29.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
people who are out there,
who are not only protesting,

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:31.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they're looking
at legislation

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.111 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and they're organizing

00:08:32.111 --> 00:08:33.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're really
getting people together.

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:35.982 line:92%
So I think if we can on our en

00:08:35.982 --> 00:08:39.986
in making things
help emotionally prepare people,

00:08:39.986 --> 00:08:41.254 line:92%
it's a good part of the process,

00:08:41.254 --> 00:08:44.357
but it's hardly the kind
of change that, you know,

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:47.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone who I admire so much
like Patrisse, is doing

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:49.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
and has been doing
since she was 15.

00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:53.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so how many years
into activism

00:08:53.332 --> 00:08:55.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
and organizing are you,
Patrisse?

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:58.471
-21 years.
I've been doing it for 21 years.

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:01.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How did people first reac
to you when --

00:09:01.674 --> 00:09:03.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess you must have
been a teenager,

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:06.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
as Ramy said, when you first
started taking this on.

00:09:06.746 --> 00:09:10.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My friends thought
I was strange,

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:12.785 line:92%
but that's not uncommon for me

00:09:12.785 --> 00:09:13.853 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I was, like, not the --

00:09:13.853 --> 00:09:17.690
I was always kind of the strange
kid doing my own thing.

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:19.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they would come with me
to events,

00:09:19.759 --> 00:09:21.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know,
friend groups,

00:09:21.294 --> 00:09:22.562 line:92%
and I would be like, "Alright.

00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:24.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
They'd be like,
Let's go do this thing."

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:26.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd be like, "Well,
let's go to this march,

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:30.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
or let's go to this meetin
about activism

00:09:30.036 --> 00:09:32.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the transit system
in Los Angeles."

00:09:32.104 --> 00:09:34.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we would be the youngest
people in the meeting

00:09:34.707 --> 00:09:36.676 line:92%
with, like, 50-year-old folks,

00:09:36.676 --> 00:09:40.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my friends would be like
"Yo, this is not it.

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:42.348 line:92%
This is not it, Patrisse."

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:43.015 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But I promise you,

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:45.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I started Black Lives
Matter seven years ago

00:09:45.384 --> 00:09:47.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when we were first
on the streets,

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:51.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of my good friends
who makes fun of me the most

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:53.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
she called me and said,
"I get it now.

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:56.395
I get why you've been doing this
for like 16 years.

00:09:56.395 --> 00:10:00.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I'll show up
to one of your protests."

00:10:00.299 --> 00:10:01.534 line:92%
So, yeah, I've always done this.

00:10:01.534 --> 00:10:03.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
My father --
You know, one of my father

00:10:03.936 --> 00:10:05.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
would tell me that I grew up
in the wrong generation.

00:10:05.671 --> 00:10:09.976
He was like, "You were suppose
to be born in the '60s or '70s

00:10:09.976 --> 00:10:11.911 line:92%
'cause clearly, you missed it.

00:10:11.911 --> 00:10:14.647 size:84% position:42%
This is not your time,"
but then we created it.

00:10:14.647 --> 00:10:18.517
We created a new movement,
and I'm so grateful for that

00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:21.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, obviously,
you want --

00:10:21.253 --> 00:10:23.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we all want
to be optimistic

00:10:23.022 --> 00:10:23.823 line:92%
of what will come with this,

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:27.093
but you know, I do think it'
important that our sadness

00:10:27.093 --> 00:10:28.227 line:92%
our anger, our frustration

00:10:28.227 --> 00:10:32.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
about what happened
to George Floyd remains.

00:10:32.231 --> 00:10:34.667 line:92%
Ramy, could you just speak

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:38.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
to what Islam teaches
about forgiving?

00:10:38.404 --> 00:10:41.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, this is something
that we talked about a bunch

00:10:41.507 --> 00:10:44.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is in Islam
kind of talking about,

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:47.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
what is the human's
biggest problem?

00:10:47.113 --> 00:10:48.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's not that
we're bad people.

00:10:48.214 --> 00:10:49.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's that we're forgetful,
that we forget.

00:10:49.915 --> 00:10:54.520
And so so much of our faith is
about, how do we remember God?

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:55.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do we remember
our higher selves?

00:10:55.755 --> 00:10:58.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do we stay connected
to the principles

00:10:58.391 --> 00:10:59.725 line:92%
that we know make us good

00:10:59.725 --> 00:11:02.795
and the ones that we know
help us serve humankind

00:11:02.795 --> 00:11:07.533
and serve ourselves in way
that, you know, surpass the ego.

00:11:07.533 --> 00:11:11.237
And I think so much of this is
challenging the ego of society

00:11:11.237 --> 00:11:14.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
challenging the supply chain
of how we get things,

00:11:14.573 --> 00:11:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
challenging the way we loo
at human life,

00:11:17.143 --> 00:11:19.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's almost
like something like

00:11:19.412 --> 00:11:20.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
what's happening outside
right now.

00:11:20.846 --> 00:11:23.883
It's not radical in the sens
that no one's heard about this

00:11:23.883 --> 00:11:27.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just us being like,
"Oh, man, we forgot, you know.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:28.554 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We forgot again."

00:11:28.554 --> 00:11:29.455 line:92%
You know, we keep forgetting

00:11:29.455 --> 00:11:30.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we really need
to step into that.

00:11:30.756 --> 00:11:36.095
And again, it's why the work
that Patrisse has been doing

00:11:36.095 --> 00:11:36.862 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is so important.

00:11:36.862 --> 00:11:38.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I want to thank you bot
for being here.

00:11:38.931 --> 00:11:42.902
Ramy, thank you so much fo
the introduction to Patrisse

00:11:42.902 --> 00:11:46.338
I hope the next time I see
both of you, it's in person.

00:11:46.338 --> 00:11:49.075 line:92%
And please do be safe out there.

00:11:49.075 --> 00:11:51.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much, Seth.
-Thanks.

